<#
.SYNOPSIS
    PowerShell Script Runner - Professional Edition
    A powerful GUI application for managing and executing PowerShell scripts

.DESCRIPTION
    PowerShell Script Runner is a comprehensive Windows Forms-based application that provides
    an intuitive graphical interface for browsing, executing, and managing PowerShell scripts.
    
    This application is designed for system administrators, developers, and power users who need
    a centralized way to organize and run their PowerShell script collection without needing to
    open PowerShell console or use the command line.

.FEATURES
    Core Features:
    • Script Browsing & Filtering: Quickly search and filter scripts from selected folders
    • Recursive Folder Scanning: Option to include scripts from all subfolders
    • Script Execution: Run scripts as current user or with administrator privileges
    • Script Parameters: Input dialog to pass arguments to scripts (Shift+Click Run or double-click)
    • Stop Script Button: Terminate running scripts with a single click
    • Real-time Monitoring: Live terminal output with color support and execution timer
    
    Organization & History:
    • Script History: Track and quick-access your 15 most recent scripts
    • Execution Log: Persistent log with success/failure status, duration, and timestamps
    • View Execution Log: Dialog to review past script runs with color-coded status
    
    Code Viewer & Editor:
    • Syntax Highlighting: Color-coded PowerShell keywords, cmdlets, variables, strings, and comments
    • Code Preview: View full script code in the integrated editor
    • Code Editor: Edit and save script modifications directly from the application
    • Copy Code: One-click copy of script content to clipboard
    
    Scheduling:
    • Script Scheduler: Schedule scripts to run at specific dates and times
    • Scheduled Tasks Manager: View, manage, and delete pending/completed tasks
    • Toast Notifications: Windows notifications when scheduled scripts complete
    
    AI Assistant (OpenAI Integration):
    • Review Script: AI-powered analysis for issues, security, and improvements
    • Improve Script: Automatically optimize and enhance existing scripts
    • Create Script: Generate new scripts from natural language descriptions
    • Ask AI: Get PowerShell coding help and answer questions
    • Secure API Key Storage: Encrypted storage for OpenAI API credentials
    
    User Interface:
    • Settings Persistence: Automatically saves window size, position, and last folder
    • Visual Running Indicators: Progress bar, terminal highlighting, and spinner during execution
    • Tooltips: Helpful hints on all buttons
    • Resizable Panels: Adjustable code viewer and terminal output sections
    
    Execution Features:
    • Admin Elevation: UAC prompt integration for administrator-level script execution
    • Elapsed Time Counter: Monitor how long scripts have been running
    • Spinner Animation: Visual feedback during script execution

.AUTHOR
    Created by Bill Ridley

.VERSION
    Professional Edition v2.1 with AI Integration

.EXAMPLES
    # Launch the application
    .\PowerShell-Script-Runner.ps1

    # Via PowerShell with execution policy bypass
    powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "PowerShell-Script-Runner.ps1"

    # Via the compiled executable (no PowerShell console required)
    .\PowerShell-Script-Runner.exe

.KEYBOARD_SHORTCUTS
    • Shift+Click Run: Open parameters dialog before running
    • Shift+Click Admin: Open parameters dialog before running as admin
    • Double-click script: Open parameters dialog and run

.SYSTEM_REQUIREMENTS
    • Windows 10 or later (for toast notifications)
    • PowerShell 5.0 or later
    • .NET Framework 4.5 or later

.USAGE
    1. Launch the application by running the .ps1 file or .exe executable
    2. Click "Browse..." to select a folder containing your PowerShell scripts (.ps1 files)
    3. Enable "Recursive" checkbox to include scripts from subfolders
    4. Scripts will appear in the left panel - select any script to view its code
    5. Click "Run" to execute as current user or "Admin" to run as administrator
    6. Hold Shift while clicking Run/Admin to enter script parameters
    7. Monitor execution in the Terminal Output panel on the right
    8. Use "Stop" button to terminate a running script at any time
    9. Click "Schedule" to run a script at a specific time
    10. Access recent scripts from the "Recent Scripts" history list
    11. Toggle between Dark and Light modes using the theme button
    12. Edit scripts inline and save changes directly to the file

.SETTINGS
    User preferences and settings are automatically saved to:
    %APPDATA%\PowerShellScriptRunner\
    
    Files stored:
    • settings.json - Theme, window size, position, last folder, recursive mode
    • execution_history.json - Log of all script executions with status
    • scheduled_tasks.json - Pending and completed scheduled tasks
    • favorites.json - Favorited/pinned scripts

.NOTES
    - All scripts execute with output capture and live display
    - Scripts must be .ps1 files to be recognized
    - Administrator elevation uses Windows UAC prompt
    - History is limited to the 15 most recent scripts
    - Execution log stores up to 100 entries
    - Settings persist across application sessions
    - Toast notifications appear for scheduled task completions

.CREDIT
    Application Design & Development: Bill Ridley
    Professional GUI Implementation with Windows Forms
    Advanced Script Management and Execution Framework

#>

